<title>THAILAND: Christiani asks for share suspension.</title>
<headline>Christiani asks for share suspension.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Christiani &amp; Nielsen (Thai) Plc said it had asked the Stock Exchange of Thailand to temporarily suspend trade in its shares so it can explain its financial situation to investors.</p>
<p>The company said in a filing to the SET it recently submitted its second quarter financial statement to the bourse, and there were some changes in its operation results.</p>
<p>&quot;It is therefore essential to the company to provide explanation to the investors and the public,&quot; the statement said.</p>
</text>
